{
  "id": "binaural-interaction",
  "term": "binaural interaction",
  "definition": "Binaural interaction is the way the auditory system combines sound information arriving at both ears, including sensitivity to differences in the timing of the sound between ears. In the source packet, it is reflected by response patterns that are strongest and fastest when timing is matched across ears and become smaller and slower as the delay between ears increases.",
